nate when exposed to sufficient energy level.)>>endobj1146 0 obj<</Dest[34 0 R/XYZ 33 391 0]/Next 1147 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1145 0 R/Title(10.3.      Possibility of Hazardous Reactions:    Hazardous polymerization will not occur.)>>endobj1145 0 obj<</Dest[34 0 R/XYZ 33 429 0]/Next 1146 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1144 0 R/Title(10.2.      Chemical Stability:    HMX is a military high explosive.  HMX has been assigned the United Nations Organization Classification of Class 1, Division 1 \(mass detonating\) based on the Department of Defense Explosives Hazard Classification Proc..\.)>>endobj1144 0 obj<</Dest[34 0 R/XYZ 33 455 0]/Next 1145 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1143 0 R/Title(10.1.      Reactivity:    Reacts violently with many chemicals causing fire and explosion hazard. Material is sensitive to friction, shock, impact, and electrostatic discharge.)>>endobj1143 0 obj<</Dest[34 0 R/XYZ 29 469 0]/Next 1144 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1142 0 R/Title(SECTION 10: STABILITY AND REACTIVITY)>>endobj1142 0 obj<</Dest[28 0 R/XYZ 33 94 0]/Next 1143 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1141 0 R/Title(9.1. Information on Basic Physical and Chemical Properties)>>endobj1141 0 obj<</Dest[28 0 R/XYZ 29 109 0]/Next 1142 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1140 0 R/Title(SECTION 9: PHYSICAL AND CHEMICAL PROPERTIES)>>endobj1140 0 obj<</Dest[28 0 R/XYZ 33 420 0]/Next 1141 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1139 0 R/Title(8.1. Control Parameters)>>endobj1139 0 obj<</Dest[28 0 R/XYZ 29 435 0]/Next 1140 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1138 0 R/Title(SECTION 8: EXPOSURE CONTROLS/PERSONAL PROTECTION)>>endobj1138 0 obj<</Dest[28 0 R/XYZ 33 633 0]/Next 1139 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1137 0 R/Title(7.2. Conditions for Safe Storage, Including Any Incompatibilities)>>endobj1137 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/XYZ 33 163 0]/Next 1138 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1136 0 R/Title(7.1. Precautions for Safe Handling)>>endobj1136 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/XYZ 29 177 0]/Next 1137 0 R/Parent 1108 0 R/Prev 1135 0 R/Title(SECTION 7: HAN